# Shared by every app image. Docker reads .dockerignore from the build CONTEXT
# root, and both apps build from the repo root (`docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`),
# so this file must stay app-agnostic: each Dockerfile COPYs only what it ships.

# Dependencies & build
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests & coverage
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report
**/e2e

# Git & env — neither image reads a .env file; the API takes its vars from the
# runtime environment and the web app bakes NEXT_PUBLIC_* in at build time
# (see refs/monorepo-docker-images.md).
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*

# Docs & IDE
docs
**/*.md
.vscode
.idea
.superpowers
.DS_Store
